// Planted fixture for the bridges' questions (10 Oct 2026): what the map records on each question a
// scheme asks. test_mechanism.py pins the answers; app/test_mechanism_lint.mjs holds the page's to
// the checker's on this file as on every other. Each state and step is here for a probe.
===
title: "Planted -- what the map says to a bridge's questions"
mechanism:
    question: "What does the levy do to health?"
    levels: [state, people]
    actors:
        gov:    {label: "Government", level: state}
        people: {label: "Shoppers", level: people}
    kinds:
        price:  {label: "A price signal", general: dear}
    states:
        levy:    {label: "The levy is imposed", actor: gov, role: intervention}
        dear:    {label: "Sugary drinks cost more", actor: people, kind: price}
        drink:   {label: "Shoppers drink less sugar", actor: people}
        health:  {label: "Health improves", actor: people, role: outcome, status: possible}
        revenue: {label: "Revenue is raised", actor: gov, role: outcome}
        smuggle: {label: "Cross-border shopping", actor: people}
        habit:   {label: "Habit", actor: people}
        ads:     {label: "Advertising", actor: gov}
        income:  {label: "Household income", actor: people}
        survey:  {label: "Survey of drinking", actor: people, measures: drink}
        sweets:  {label: "Sweets cost more", actor: people, kind: price}
    chains:
        levy:
            label: "The levy's route to health"
            question: "How would the levy improve health?"
            order: explanation
===

[Levy raises prices]: The levy makes sugary drinks dearer.
    {causes: {from: levy, to: dear, sign: "+", basis: study, unless: smuggle, regime: "in towns", chain: levy, scope: general}}

[Dear drinks cut sugar]: Dearer drinks mean less sugar drunk.
    {causes: {from: dear, to: drink, sign: "-", basis: asserted, via: [habit], period: "after 2018", measured_by: survey, jointly: income, given: ["where no substitute is sold"], chain: levy}}

[Less sugar, better health]: Less sugar improves health.
    {causes: {from: drink, to: health, sign: "-", basis: asserted, scope: singular, chain: levy}}

[Habit says otherwise]: Some say habit keeps shoppers drinking. #reported
    {causes: {from: habit, to: drink, sign: "+", basis: asserted, stance: rejected}}

[Advertising pushes drinking]: Advertising raises how much is drunk.
    {causes: {from: ads, to: drink, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}

[Levy raises revenue]: The levy raises revenue.
    {causes: {from: levy, to: revenue, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}

[Levy prompts smuggling]: The levy prompts cross-border shopping.
    {causes: {from: levy, to: smuggle, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}

[Income drives both]: Income moves both prices paid and drinking.
    {causes: [{from: income, to: dear, sign: "+", basis: asserted}, {from: income, to: drink, sign: "+", basis: asserted}]}

[Drinking props up prices]: Heavy drinking keeps prices up.
    {causes: {from: drink, to: dear, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}

[Dearer in villages too]: In villages, too, the levy makes drinks dearer.
    {causes: {from: levy, to: dear, sign: "+", basis: asserted, regime: "in villages"}}

[Sweets dearer too]: Sweets cost more as well.
    {causes: {from: levy, to: sweets, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}

<Cause to effect>

(1) [Levy raises prices]
(2) [Dear drinks cut sugar]
-- From cause to effect {uses: [1, 2]} --
(3) [Sugar falls]: Sugar drunk falls.

<What to do>

(1) [Levy raises prices]
(2) [Dear drinks cut sugar]
(3) [Less sugar, better health]
-- From a mechanism to what to do {uses: [1, 2, 3]} --
(4) [Impose the levy]: The government should impose the levy.

<Correlation>

(1) [Dear drinks cut sugar]
-- From correlation to cause {uses: [1]} --
(2) [Price drives drinking]: Price drives drinking.

<Effect to cause>

(1) [Dear drinks cut sugar]
-- From effect to cause {uses: [1]} --
(2) [Price explains the fall]: Price explains the fall in drinking.

<Lever>

(1) [Less sugar, better health]
-- From a mechanism to a possibility {uses: [1]} --
(2) [Health can improve]: Health can be improved.

<Cases>

(1) [Levy raises prices]
(2) [Sweets dearer too]
-- From cases to a general mechanism {uses: [1, 2]} --
(3) [Levies raise prices]: Levies raise prices.

<Theory>

(1) [Less sugar, better health]
-- From a mechanism against a theory {uses: [1]} --
(2) [Choice theory fails]: The theory of free choice fails here.

<There to here>

(1) [Levy raises prices]
(2) [Dear drinks cut sugar]
(3) [Dearer in villages too]
-- From there to here {uses: [1, 2, 3]} --
(4) [It would work in villages]: The levy would cut sugar in villages too.

<Vindication>

(1) [Levy raises prices]
-- Vindicatory genealogy {uses: [1]} --
(2) [The levy is warranted]: The levy meets needs we have.
